<p class="px-2">
    The Pigpen cipher is a simple substitution cipher where each letter is represented by a symbol formed from parts of a grid. These symbols use straight or angled lines, and may include a dot to distinguish characters. Type a message to see it in glyphs, or tap the glyphs you see to read them as letters. "Save as image" downloads the glyphs as a picture.
</p>
<p class="px-2">
     There is more information available on the <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pigpen_cipher" class="text-convrtr">Pigpen cipher</a> Wikipedia page. 
</p>
